column2070:
Oct 23, 2020 11:21;637dc53b5fce844d60686df5;Customer Alibaba did raise a trouble ticket on our circuit HKG(PCG)-HKG(PCG) NP10108, about the circuit unstable issue.
The circuit is a Dark Fiber cable HKG local loop, between KwaiChung/MCX-10 & Fanling/OLK(HKG71). Data bandwidth is 100Gbps. Ethernet.
2020-10-22@12:30pm, I arrived Fanling/OLK site.
The circuit is an OFF-NET which is provided by HKT local team.

At HKT's MMR at 4th floor of OLK/HKG71 site, I checked the signal power level: -
@1550nm.  RX= -18.20dBm. from MCX-10
@1330nm.  RX= -18.39dBm. from MCX-10
@1330nm.  RX= +03.82dBm. from OLK/HKG71

Further checking at Alibaba's PoP site, Rack E04/U3@3/floor: -
@1550nm. RX= -18.31dBm. from MCX-10
@1310nm. RX= -18.41dBm. from MCX-10
@1310nm. RX= +03.76dBm. from OLK/HKG71.

By above checked figures, we noted that the OLK/HKG71's in-house cross-connect has NO problem.  and the whole HKG local loop is good under our specification.
The customer Alibaba told us that they saw from their port via NMS the RX was -21.8dBm only which signal is too low. (but we checked its real value is -18.20dBm.)

The customer agreed our opinion:  we suspected that customer's equipment port/SFP performance could be deteriorated or having issues.

